# Path A string ops (owned) — product floor + residual honesty

**Status:** Path A product free names **In** (alpha).  
**Marker:** `STR_OPS_PATH_A_ALPHA`  
**Mission:** M165 — deepen native string ops without claiming true borrowed `&str` lifetimes.

## Path A free names (In)

| Free name | Result | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| `str_starts_with(s, pre)` | `Bool` | Byte prefix match |
| `str_ends_with(s, suf)` | `Bool` | Byte suffix match |
| `str_index_of(s, sub)` | `Int` | First **byte** index of `sub`, or **-1** if missing |
| `str_repeat(s, n)` | `String` | Owned concat × n; **cap n≤1024** + `len*n` soft safety |
| `str_to_uppercase(s)` | `String` | Owned ASCII upper copy |

**Already present (not new this mission):**

- Method `s.to_lowercase()` / runtime `oo_str_to_lowercase` (owned)
- Method `s.trim()`, free `str_slice` / `char_at` / `str_contains` / concat / len

Runtime symbols: `oo_str_starts_with`, `oo_str_ends_with`, `oo_str_index_of`, `oo_str_repeat`, `oo_str_to_uppercase` (`chs_rt_str.c` / `chs_rt_print.c`).

## std product wrappers

`std/str.oo` / `std/core/str.oo` thin wrappers (pure path): `starts_with`, `ends_with`, `index_of`, `repeat`, `to_uppercase` → free names above.

## What is true today

| Layer | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| **Types** | Product string is owned **`String`** (`OoStr` + ARC). |
| **Search / slice** | Byte-index ops on owned values; results are **new** owned `String` or `Int`/`Bool`. |
| **Case map** | ASCII `tolower`/`toupper` owned copies — not Unicode case folding. |

## Residual honesty (do **not** claim)

- Native **`&str`** borrow with lifetimes / shared non-owning views
- Zero-copy slice that outlives the parent without retain-release
- UTF-8-aware `index_of` / case map as DESIGN-done (byte / ASCII only here)
- Elimination of string value-copy overhead via true borrow

True `&str` borrow / lifetimes remain residual — see also `bootstrap/BYTE_STR.oot`.

